content:
Simply use `this.router` in Pinia stores to get access to the router.

Here is an example:

```js
import { defineStore } from 'pinia'

export const useWhateverStore = defineStore('whatever', {
  // ...
  actions: {
    whateverAction () { // do NOT use arrow function
      this.router.push('...')
    }
  }
}
```
